    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Look.</strong> Groundskeeper and gravedigger, 60s. Stooped, mud to the knees, smells of pond water and pipe smoke. Scarecrow-patched coat, lantern, a shovel he never puts down.</p><p><strong>Wants.</strong> Elspeth to rest in peace.</p><p><strong>Secret.</strong> Every Hallows' Eve he lights warding lanterns around the pond; he was there 8:30-9:00. Decades ago he helped brick up part of an old passage under the house.</p><p><strong>Knows.</strong> The passage runs from the chapel crypt up to the master's study, behind the bookshelves. Two scarecrows are missing (C9). Shares it if the party helps with his lanterns, respects the legend, or wins Insight/Persuasion DC 13.</p><p><strong>Plays as.</strong> Gruff and slow, spits between sentences, lowers his voice at any mention of the pond. With the Why Edge he and Edric hold the coffin lids shut.</p><p><strong>Lines.</strong></p><ul><li>“Mind the pond. She's restless tonight.”</li><li>“She walks every Hallows' Eve. Never hurt a soul. Not till now, they'll say. They'll be wrong.”</li></ul>",
        "public": ""
      },
